Package: pliman
Title: Tools for Plant Image Analysis
Version: 3.2.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Tiago", "Olivoto", , "tiagoolivoto@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-0241-9636"))
Description: An all-in-one computer vision and machine learning ecosystem for
    plant phenomics, digital agriculture, and phytopathometry (Olivoto, 2022
    <doi:10.1111/2041-210X.13803>; Olivoto et al., 2022
    <doi:10.1007/s40858-021-00487-5>). Provides high-throughput single-
    and batch-image workflows for leaf area quantification, seed and grain
    counting, disease severity scoring, color indexes, shape analysis,
    landmark identification, and Elliptical Fourier Analysis of outlines
    (Claude, 2008 <doi:10.1007/978-0-387-77789-4>). Supports field-scale
    phenotyping from UAV and satellite RGB, multispectral, and hyperspectral
    orthomosaics with automated plot-grid shapefile layout design. Integrates
    state-of-the-art deep learning architectures (YOLO, Segment Anything,
    Grounded-SAM, PerSAM, StarDist, CLIP) for zero-shot and custom object
    detection, instance segmentation, SAHI high-resolution tiling, automated
    labeling, dataset curation, model training, and asynchronous parallel 
    batch inference.
